<title>DENMARK: Danish June new car sales fell 37.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Danish June new car sales fell 37.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish new car registrations fell 37.8 percent in June 1997 to 8,050 from 12,943 a year earlier, the Automobile Importers' Society said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The society attributed the fall to the effect of higher car taxes which took effect on June 1, 1997 and noted that May registrations had shown a dramatic rise as buyers apparently rushed to beat the deadline.</p>
<p>				     June 1997   June 1996</p>
<p>    New car registrations	 8,050    12,943</p>
<p>Leading May registrations by manufacturer</p>
<p>    Volkswagen AG	 1,563</p>
<p>    General Motors Corp     847</p>
<p>    Ford Motor Co	    601</p>
<p>    Toyota		  326</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen Newsroom, +45-33-969650</p>
